WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Alex Rivera: Morning everyone. Let's run through where we are on the notifications feature before sprint ends Friday.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Jordan Patel: Backend's mostly there. The one thing holding me up is we're still waiting on Twilio to increase our rate limit — I opened a support ticket four days ago and haven't heard back. Can't load-test the SMS path until that's resolved.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Alex Rivera: Okay, that's a real blocker. I'll escalate with our Twilio account rep today and see if I can get someone on the phone.

4
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Kim Osei: On the frontend side, the notification settings UI is basically done, just waiting on Jordan's endpoint to wire it up for real data. Right now I'm working off mocked responses.

5
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Jordan Patel: I can have the endpoint ready for you by Wednesday even without the Twilio fix, since that only affects the SMS channel — email and push should work fine.

6
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Kim Osei: Perfect, that unblocks me. I'll have the full UI wired up and ready for QA by Thursday then.

7
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Sam Torres: Speaking of QA, I found a bug yesterday where push notifications are being sent twice if the user has multiple devices registered. Logged it in the tracker already.

8
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Jordan Patel: Yeah, I saw that. I think it's a dedup issue in the fan-out job. I can take that one, should be a quick fix — I'll get a patch up tomorrow.

9
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Alex Rivera: Great. Sam, once Kim's UI is ready Thursday, can you run a full QA pass before we cut the release Friday morning?

10
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Sam Torres: Yep, I'll block off Thursday afternoon for that.

11
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:34.000
Alex Rivera: One more thing — Kim, did you get a chance to look at the accessibility audit feedback from last week?

12
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Kim Osei: Not yet, honestly it's been lower priority with the notifications work. I can look at it next week once this ships.

13
00:01:42.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Alex Rivera: That's fine, no rush on that one. Okay, let's recap — I'm escalating the Twilio ticket today, Jordan's getting the endpoint to Kim by Wednesday and fixing the duplicate-notification bug by tomorrow, Kim's wiring up the UI by Thursday, and Sam's doing full QA Thursday afternoon before Friday's release. Sound good?

14
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.000
Jordan Patel: Sounds good.

15
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Kim Osei: Yep.

16
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Sam Torres: All set.
